# E2E test infrastructure — test harness code, not production paths.
# Semgrep flags template literals passed to console.warn (unsafe-format-
# string false positives on JS template literals) and non-literal-regex
# false positives where the input is a hard-coded config key. Neither
# has an attacker-reachable input surface.
ui/e2e/

# Dev tooling — not shipped, not run against untrusted input.
scripts/
eval/

# Build output.
ui/dist/
**/node_modules/
agent/wheels/
infra/.build/
infra/.terraform/

# Terraform is covered by Checkov + TFLint (see .checkov.yaml,
# .tflint.hcl). Semgrep's terraform ruleset duplicates the CMK / KMS
# hardening set we've reasoned through in .checkov.yaml, so run
# those tools instead and skip Semgrep here to avoid double reporting.
infra/
